%I A400077 #6 Nov 24 2026 21:27:21
%S A400077 1,9,25,97,313,1041,3529,11553,38937,128817
%N A400077 Number of nonzero terms in 1 - Product_{uv in E(G)} (1 - x_u*x_v) reduced modulo x_i^2 = x_i for the ladder graph G = P_2 X P_n.
%C A400077 For any nonempty vertex subset S of G = P_2 X P_n, the coefficient of Product_{i in S} x_i is (-1)^(|S|+1) * I(G[S]; -1), where I(H; x) is the independence polynomial of H (a special case of signed domination in reliability theory), so a(n) counts the nonempty subsets S with I(G[S]; -1) != 0.
%C A400077 Note that a(2) = A400076(4) = 9, since P_2 X P_2 is isomorphic to the cycle graph C_4.
%H A400077 A. Satyanarayana and A. Prabhakar, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TR.1978.5220266">New Topological Formula and Rapid Algorithm for Reliability Analysis of Complex Networks</a>, IEEE Transactions on Reliability, R-27 (1978), 82-100.
%e A400077 For n = 1, P_2 X P_1 is a single edge, so 1 - (1 - x1*x2) = x1*x2, which has 1 nonzero term, giving a(1) = 1.
%Y A400077 Cf. A203175, A400076.
%K A400077 nonn,more,new
%O A400077 1,2
